    <h2>What still exists elsewhere</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.facebook.com/lAg0rA">facebook.com/lAg0rA</a>: L'AgorA's page, with its albums ("L'Ag0rA de A @ Z", "L'AgorA, from ground up", "What is l'AgorA (Archives 2011)", "Célébration du solstice d'hiver", "les champignons", "A2g0r1A2"), its past events and its 426 posts, from July 2010 to today.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.facebook.com/EarthdanceQc">Earthdance St-Fortunat</a>, the page of the 2012 to 2014 editions.</li>
      <li>The Facebook group "L'Agora" (766 members) and the group "Co-voiturage // Ride-share → AgorA" (248 members).</li>
      <li>The Agora's profile on rave.ca, "memories with photos".</li>
      <li>The domain ag0ra.org, registered on December 14, 2012, still the collective's. The domain ledonjon.ca, for its part, has been free for years.</li>
      <li>In the <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/*/ledonjon.ca*">Wayback Machine</a>: 56 captures of ledonjon.ca between March 7, 2010 and May 2, 2019, and 47 captures of ag0ra.org since August 18, 2013. The address ag0ra.dyndns.org, used for a time, was never captured.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What went into making this site</h2>
    <p>A folder of 2,659 files, 2.3 GB, kept on a hard drive: the backups of the two websites, the brochures and their source files, the plans, the Donjon's calendars, the posters, the photos from 2009 to 2014 (with their capture dates), four videos, the contracts and administrative documents (not published), the files submitted to the agricultural land protection commission and to the municipality (not published), and the maps of the land. Plus the Facebook page, re-read post by post to reconstruct the <a href="/en/timeline/">timeline</a>. Plus the Wayback Machine's captures, for the versions of ledonjon.ca the hard drive did not have.</p>
    <p>The quoted texts are reproduced as written, with their spelling; on the English pages, French originals are translated, and quotations that were originally in English are given as they were. People are named by first name or artist name, as they appeared publicly at the time; personal addresses, numbers and email addresses were removed. The owner of the land is not named.</p>
  </div>
